// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// JOB TEMPLATES — default library (v2)
// 107 pre-built job/quote templates. Consumed by job-templates.js
// (window.JobTemplates), which resolves items through EstimateLogic —
// coded items reference the xactimate/labor catalogs (CI-validated by
// tests/job-templates.test.js: every code must resolve).
// Pure data — no behavior. Custom/tenant templates layer on top via
// localStorage (see job-templates.js); this array is never mutated.
//
// NO COST DATA LIVES HERE (2026-08-18). Until this version, each of the
// 84 `custom` line items carried materialCost + laborCost — 146 non-zero
// contractor figures, published unauthenticated at /pro/js/
// job-templates-data.js and from raw.githubusercontent.com, next to a
// public estimate-logic-engine.js carrying the markup math. Cost basis
// and margin were both derivable. See documentation/audit/
// JOB-TEMPLATE-COST-LEAK-2026-08-18.md.
//
// A custom item now publishes its SCOPE only — name, desc, unit, qty,
// category — which the homeowner sees on the estimate anyway. Its cost
// is TENANT-OWNED, at catalogCosts/{companyId}.jtCosts, keyed
// 'jt-<slug(templateId)>-<index>'. The split, the key, and the
// validation live in functions/job-template-cost-logic.js;
// docs/pro/js/catalog-costs.js fetches the book and job-templates.js
// bridges it onto the line items.
//
// A TENANT WITH NO COST BOOK HAS NO COSTS. Those items resolve at an
// explicit 0 flagged `costUnset: true`, and the UI renders "Cost not
// set" / "—" rather than a price. The explicit zero is not cosmetic:
// estimate-logic-engine.js:803 resolves a labor id BEFORE testing
// `laborCost != null`, so OMITTING the key routes 14 of these items to
// a public NBD_LABOR rate and fabricates a confident wrong price.
//
// WARRANTY KIND + TIER FLAG (2026-09-25). Every template carries an explicit
// `warrantyKind` — the workmanship warranty its paperwork prints, years from
// NBD_ESTIMATE_CONFIG.WORKMANSHIP_WARRANTY:
//   roof            roofing replacements — the existing tier wording, unchanged
//   gutter_system   a new gutter system (5 yr)
//   guard_only      leaf protection on existing gutters (2 yr)
//   install_default every other install/replacement (2 yr, Jo's proposals)
//   repair          1 yr ONLY if the rep ticks the box on that estimate —
//                   includes temporary emergency work (tarp, leak stopgap,
//                   board-up): it prints none by default, the same as 'none',
//                   but the rep keeps Jo's per-job choice (review 2026-09-25)
//   none            inspections, documentation, cleaning, washing, moss
//                   treatment — no workmanship to warrant, so no box
// Set per template on purpose, not derived from category or jobType: a
// downspout-only package is an install but not a new gutter system; a tune-up
// is "maintenance" but does repair work. Review a new template's kind here.
//
// `tierPriced: true` shows the Good/Better/Best row in the Job Templates build
// screen. No template sets it: every template resolves to the same total at
// all three tiers, and a tier row that prices nothing only printed
// "Preferred" on paperwork. Set it on a template only once its tier really
// changes the price (the planned roofing ladder).
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

