{"id":"jt_sp_modbit_lowslope","name":"Modified Bitumen Low-Slope Roof","category":"specialty_roofing","jobType":"replacement","warrantyKind":"roof","description":"Replacement of your low-slope or flat roof section with a two-ply modified bitumen system, including new edge metal and sealed pipe penetrations.","scopeNotes":"Full-job template: rep enters real measurements. Two-ply mod bit default; mineral-surface rolled roofing available as the budget option on porches/additions only - warn on lifespan. Tear-off is a CUSTOM line sized for a typical 15 SQ section - ADJUST QTY (no catalog code for low-slope tear-off). Parapet cap is optional, keyed to wall LF. Great template for the low-slope section of a mixed roof - pair with a shingle replacement template and the shared overhead lines (MOB/DEMOB/dumpsters/permit) dedupe automatically. Excludes decking, tapered insulation, and interior repairs.","tags":["modified bitumen","low slope","flat roof","replacement"],"durationHint":"1-2 days","minJobCharge":null,"measurements":null,"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Tear off existing low-slope roofing","desc":"Remove existing low-slope roofing to deck, load out","unit":"SQ","qty":15,"category":"labor"}},{"code":"RFG MOD-BIT","brandOptions":[{"label":"Modified Bitumen 2-Ply","code":"RFG MOD-BIT"},{"label":"Rolled Roofing (Mineral Surface)","code":"RFG ROLLED"}]},{"code":"RFG DRPE-AL"},{"code":"RFG PARAP","optional":true},{"code":"RFG PIPE-STD"},{"code":"DSP 20YD"},{"code":"DSP 30YD"},{"code":"DSP 40YD"},{"code":"PRM RES-OH"},{"code":"LAB DEMOB"},{"code":"LAB CLN-M"},{"code":"MAT DEL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_sp_tile_repair_10","name":"Tile Roof Repair - ~10 Tiles","category":"specialty_roofing","jobType":"repair","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Careful removal and replacement of around ten cracked or slipped roof tiles, including fresh underlayment in the repair area and haul-away of the broken pieces.","scopeNotes":"Fixed-scope repair sized for ~10 tiles (about a quarter square). Concrete tile default, clay available - MATCH THE PROFILE before quoting; sourcing discontinued profiles is a change order. Detail hours cover walking pads, careful extraction, and re-bedding. Includes a felt patch under the repair area only. Excludes full underlayment replacement (the real failure point on 20+ year tile roofs - quote a lift-and-relay if felt is gone), batten replacement, and ridge mortar work. If more than ~20 tiles are broken, stop and re-scope as a slope repair.","tags":["tile","repair","concrete","clay"],"durationHint":"2-4 hours","minJobCharge":750,"measurements":{"rawSqft":50,"pitch":5,"waste":1.15,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"RFG TILE-CON","qty":0.25,"brandOptions":[{"label":"Concrete Tile","code":"RFG TILE-CON"},{"label":"Clay Tile","code":"RFG TILE-CLAY"}]},{"code":"RFG 30F","qty":0.5},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":3},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_sp_slate_repair_10","name":"Slate Roof Repair - ~10 Pieces","category":"specialty_roofing","jobType":"repair","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Replacement of around ten broken or missing slates using slate hooks and copper bibs, matched as closely as possible to your existing roof.","scopeNotes":"Fixed-scope repair sized for ~10 slates (about a quarter square). Natural slate default; synthetic composite slate offered where an exact color/size match is impossible or budget-driven. Hooks and copper bibs are a custom line (no catalog code). Detail hours assume steep, fragile access - roof jacks line is optional, keep it on 9/12+ or 2-story work. Excludes flashing/valley rebuilds (the usual real leak source on slate - inspect and quote separately), structural work, and any walking-damage liability on brittle 80+ year roofs; photograph existing broken slates before starting. 10+ broken pieces per slope means end-of-life - pivot to replacement conversation.","tags":["slate","repair","historic","premium"],"durationHint":"3-5 hours","minJobCharge":850,"measurements":{"rawSqft":50,"pitch":9,"waste":1.15,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":2,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"RFG SLATE-NAT","qty":0.25,"brandOptions":[{"label":"Natural Slate","code":"RFG SLATE-NAT"},{"label":"Synthetic Slate (Composite)","code":"RFG SLATE-SYN"}]},{"custom":{"name":"Slate hooks & copper bibs","desc":"Stainless slate hooks and copper bib flashings for each replacement slate","unit":"EA","qty":10,"category":"roofing"}},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":4},{"code":"EQP RJ","qty":1,"optional":true},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_sp_porch_metal_accent","name":"Porch / Accent Standing Seam Metal Roof","category":"specialty_roofing","jobType":"install","warrantyKind":"install_default","description":"Tear-off and installation of a standing seam metal accent roof on your porch or entry, including high-temperature underlayment, matching trim, and flashing where the roof meets the wall.","scopeNotes":"Fixed-scope install sized for a ~200 SF porch (2 SQ). Metal choices: 24ga steel default, aluminum, Galvalume. Headwall flashing LF and drip edge LF are baked for a 20 ft x 10 ft porch - adjust to actual perimeter. On-site bending hours cover custom eave/rake trim to match the accent profile. Assumes one layer of comp shingle tear-off; low-slope porches under 2/12 should go mod bit or membrane instead, not standing seam. Excludes ceiling/framing repair (add LAB CARP), gutter rework, and painting. Great add-on line while doing a main-roof replacement - sell the curb appeal.","tags":["metal","porch","accent","standing seam","install"],"durationHint":"1 day","minJobCharge":950,"measurements":{"rawSqft":200,"pitch":3,"waste":1.15,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":20,"rakeLf":16,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":12,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"LAB TO1","qty":2},{"code":"RFG METAL-SS24","qty":2,"brandOptions":[{"label":"Standing Seam 24ga Steel","code":"RFG METAL-SS24"},{"label":"Standing Seam Aluminum","code":"RFG METAL-SSAL"},{"label":"Standing Seam Galvalume","code":"RFG METAL-GAL"}]},{"code":"RFG SYN-HT","qty":2},{"code":"RFG IWS-HT","qty":1},{"code":"RFG DRPE-AL","qty":36},{"code":"RFG HDWL","qty":12},{"code":"LAB BND-M","qty":2},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_sp_flat_roof_coating","name":"Flat Roof Coating / Restoration","category":"specialty_roofing","jobType":"maintenance","warrantyKind":"install_default","description":"Restoration of your existing flat roof with a seamless waterproof coating: we pressure wash the surface, reinforce every seam and penetration, then apply two coats of high-solids roof coating to extend the roof's life for years.","scopeNotes":"Fixed-scope restoration sized for a ~15 SQ flat roof - ADJUST the three custom lines (wash, seam reinforcement, coating) to actual squares and seam LF. Silicone is the default system (ponding-water safe); swap the coating line description/cost for elastomeric acrylic on sloped-to-drain roofs where budget matters. All coating lines are custom - no coating products exist in the catalog. Only quote over sound, dry substrate: do core cuts first; saturated insulation kills adhesion and the warranty - pivot to jt_sp_tpo_flat_full if wet. Includes retrofit boots on 2 pipes. Excludes membrane repairs beyond seam reinforcement, wet insulation replacement, and interior repairs. Upsell: annual maintenance inspection.","tags":["coating","silicone","flat roof","restoration","maintenance"],"durationHint":"1-2 days","minJobCharge":950,"measurements":{"rawSqft":1500,"pitch":1,"waste":1.05,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":40,"pipes":2,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Pressure wash & surface prep","desc":"Pressure wash roof field, let dry, spot-prime per coating manufacturer spec","unit":"SQ","qty":15,"category":"labor"}},{"custom":{"name":"Seam & penetration reinforcement","desc":"Polyester mesh embedded in flashing-grade base coat at all seams, curbs and penetrations","unit":"LF","qty":60,"category":"roofing"}},{"code":"RFG PIPE-RTR","qty":2},{"custom":{"name":"Silicone restoration coating (2 coats)","desc":"High-solids silicone roof coating, two coats to manufacturer mil spec; elastomeric acrylic available","unit":"SQ","qty":15,"category":"roofing"}},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_se_emergency_tarp","name":"Emergency Tarp Install","category":"storm_emergency","jobType":"emergency","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Rapid-response tarp installation to cover storm-damaged roof areas and stop water from entering your home until permanent repairs are made.","scopeNotes":"Covers up to ~4 SQ of damaged roof with secured heavy-duty tarping. Includes insurance photo documentation of the damage BEFORE covering it — do not skip. EMR MOB adder is toggleable for after-hours/weekend response. Excludes permanent repair, debris hauling beyond loose pickup, and interior water mitigation (quote EMR WTR separately). Upsell: full storm inspection package (jt_se_storm_inspection) and the permanent section repair.","tags":["storm","tarp","emergency","leak","insurance"],"durationHint":"1-2 hours","minJobCharge":500,"measurements":{"rawSqft":400,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB","qty":1},{"code":"EMR MOB","qty":1,"optional":true},{"code":"EMR TRP","qty":4},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"code":"DSP DBR-H","qty":1,"optional":true},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1,"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_se_leak_stopgap","name":"Emergency Leak Stopgap + Assessment","category":"storm_emergency","jobType":"emergency","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Same-day temporary sealing of an active roof leak plus a full damage assessment, so your home stays dry while a permanent repair is planned.","scopeNotes":"Emergency dry-in of the active leak point (sealant/patch/small tarp via LAB WATR-D) plus initial damage inspection and photo documentation for a possible claim. Detail hours cover chasing the leak path and temporary sealing. This is a STOPGAP — always pair with a permanent repair quote. Excludes interior drywall/paint (quote INT codes separately). EMR MOB toggleable for after-hours.","tags":["leak","emergency","stopgap","assessment","storm"],"durationHint":"2-3 hours","minJobCharge":500,"measurements":{"rawSqft":100,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":1,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB","qty":1},{"code":"EMR MOB","qty":1,"optional":true},{"code":"LAB WATR-D","qty":1},{"code":"EMR INS","qty":1},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":2},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1,"optional":true},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1,"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_se_tree_impact","name":"Tree Impact — Debris Removal + Deck Patch","category":"storm_emergency","jobType":"emergency","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Safe removal of a fallen tree or large limbs from your roof, cleanup of the debris, and a structural patch of the damaged roof deck with temporary weatherproofing.","scopeNotes":"Tree/limb removal from roof, emergency debris cleanup, ~3 sheets (96 SF) OSB deck patch, synthetic dry-in over the patch, and tarp cover until permanent shingle repair. Structural rafter/truss repair hours are toggleable — confirm on-site. Photo documentation included (insurance claims almost always apply). Excludes stump/yard tree work (refer arborist), permanent shingle install (quote jt_se_wind_section_repair or a replacement), and interior repairs. Two haul loads included; large canopies may need a dumpster instead.","tags":["tree","storm","emergency","deck","debris","insurance"],"durationHint":"4-8 hours","minJobCharge":1500,"measurements":{"rawSqft":300,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":30,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB","qty":1},{"code":"EMR TREE","qty":1},{"code":"EMR DBR","qty":1},{"code":"RFG OSB716","qty":96},{"code":"RFG STRUCT","qty":2,"optional":true},{"code":"RFG SYN","qty":1,"brandOptions":[{"label":"Synthetic Underlayment Standard","code":"RFG SYN"},{"label":"TAMKO Synthetic Guard","code":"RFG SYN-TAMKO"}]},{"code":"EMR TRP","qty":1},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":2}]},
{"id":"jt_se_storm_inspection","name":"Storm Damage Inspection & Documentation Package","category":"storm_emergency","jobType":"inspection","warrantyKind":"none","description":"A thorough post-storm roof inspection with a complete photo record and written damage summary you can hand directly to your insurance company.","scopeNotes":"Full-roof storm inspection: shingles, flashings, vents, gutters, soft metals. Detail hours cover test squares, chalk marking, measurements, and the written damage summary. Drone flight is toggleable for steep/2-story roofs. Fee is commonly credited back if the customer signs a repair/replacement contract — confirm current promo before promising. Excludes tarping or any repair work. Upsell: adjuster walk support (jt_se_adjuster_walk) once a claim is filed.","tags":["inspection","storm","hail","wind","insurance","documentation"],"durationHint":"1-2 hours","minJobCharge":350,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2000,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":40,"eaveLf":60,"rakeLf":40,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":0,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB","qty":1},{"code":"EMR INS","qty":1},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":2},{"custom":{"name":"Drone photo flight","desc":"Aerial photo set of all slopes for steep or multi-story roofs","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"documentation"},"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_se_adjuster_walk","name":"Insurance Adjuster Walk Support","category":"storm_emergency","jobType":"inspection","warrantyKind":"none","description":"Your contractor walks the roof with the insurance adjuster to point out all storm damage, so nothing is missed on your claim.","scopeNotes":"On-site representation during the carrier's adjuster inspection: walk every slope with the adjuster, flag hail hits and wind creases, set test squares, and photo-document everything the adjuster sees (and anything they skip) for later supplements. Detail hours cover chalking and side-by-side scope comparison. Schedule ONLY after the adjuster appointment is confirmed. Excludes report writing — pair with jt_se_supplement_docs if the carrier scope comes back short.","tags":["insurance","adjuster","claim","storm","advocacy"],"durationHint":"2-3 hours","minJobCharge":350,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2000,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":40,"eaveLf":60,"rakeLf":40,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":0,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB","qty":1},{"code":"LAB WALK","qty":1},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":2}]},
{"id":"jt_se_wind_section_repair","name":"Wind Claim Section Repair (insurance-documented)","category":"storm_emergency","jobType":"repair","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Tear-off and re-shingle of a wind-damaged roof section, with complete before-and-after photo documentation for your insurance claim.","scopeNotes":"Sized for a ~3 SQ slope section: tear off, synthetic underlayment, architectural shingles, starter at the eave, and ridge cap. CUP DRPE and CUP IWS-E are code-upgrade lines — include when local code requires and the carrier owes them (itemize on the supplement if denied). Full photo documentation + final QC walk included. Match shingle brand/color to the existing roof via brand options; warn the customer about weathering mismatch on older roofs. Excludes decking replacement beyond incidental (add RFG OSB716) and gutter/fascia damage (separate templates).","tags":["wind","repair","insurance","shingle","storm","claim"],"durationHint":"1 day","minJobCharge":1000,"measurements":{"rawSqft":300,"pitch":6,"waste":1.15,"ridgeLf":15,"eaveLf":35,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB","qty":1},{"code":"LAB TO1","qty":3},{"code":"RFG SYN","qty":3,"brandOptions":[{"label":"Synthetic Underlayment Standard","code":"RFG SYN"},{"label":"TAMKO Synthetic Guard","code":"RFG SYN-TAMKO"},{"label":"30lb Felt (match existing)","code":"RFG 30F"}]},{"code":"RFG 240-GAF-HDZ","qty":3,"brandOptions":[{"label":"GAF Timberline HDZ","code":"RFG 240-GAF-HDZ"},{"label":"Owens Corning Duration","code":"RFG 240-OC-DUR"},{"label":"TAMKO Titan XT (Impact Class 3)","code":"RFG 240-TAMKO-TITAN"},{"label":"CertainTeed Landmark Pro","code":"RFG 240-CT-LMP"}]},{"code":"RFG STRT","qty":35},{"code":"RFG RIDG-ARC","qty":15,"brandOptions":[{"label":"Ridge Cap Architectural","code":"RFG RIDG-ARC"},{"label":"TAMKO Hip & Ridge","code":"RFG RIDG-TAMKO"},{"label":"Impact-Rated Ridge Cap","code":"RFG RIDG-IMP"}]},{"code":"CUP DRPE","qty":35,"optional":true},{"code":"CUP IWS-E","qty":35,"optional":true},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"code":"LAB WALK","qty":1},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_se_board_up_dry_in","name":"Board-Up / Temporary Dry-In","category":"storm_emergency","jobType":"emergency","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Emergency boarding of damaged openings and temporary waterproof covering of the roof, securing your home against weather and entry until repairs begin.","scopeNotes":"Board-up of broken windows/openings (~2 sheets OSB) plus ~2 SQ tarp dry-in over roof punctures; carpentry hours cover framing/blocking to fasten boards. Photo-document all damage BEFORE covering. EMR MOB toggleable for after-hours response. Excludes glass replacement, permanent roof repair, and interior water extraction (EMR WTR). Most of these become insurance claims — capture the claim number at the door.","tags":["board-up","dry-in","emergency","storm","securing"],"durationHint":"2-4 hours","minJobCharge":650,"measurements":{"rawSqft":200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB","qty":1},{"code":"EMR MOB","qty":1,"optional":true},{"code":"EMR BRD","qty":1},{"code":"RFG OSB716","qty":64},{"code":"EMR TRP","qty":2},{"code":"LAB CARP","qty":2},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1,"optional":true},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1,"optional":true},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1,"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_se_ice_dam_retrofit","name":"Ice Dam Removal + Ice & Water Shield Retrofit","category":"storm_emergency","jobType":"repair","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Safe steam removal of ice dams from your roof edge, then an ice-and-water barrier retrofit under the eave shingles to stop the leaks from coming back.","scopeNotes":"Steam removal only — NEVER hatchets or salt on shingles. Retrofit scope: tear back ~1.5 SQ of eave-course shingles along ~40 LF of eave, install self-adhered ice & water membrane, re-shingle. Drip edge replacement toggleable (often bent by ice). Heat cable is the prevention upsell — pitch it while the damage is fresh. Ice dams signal attic insulation/ventilation problems: recommend a ventilation assessment (CUP VNT-R) as follow-up. Steam work is weather-dependent; retrofit may need a return trip in hard freeze.","tags":["ice dam","winter","eave","retrofit","leak"],"durationHint":"1 day","minJobCharge":900,"measurements":{"rawSqft":150,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":40,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB","qty":1},{"custom":{"name":"Ice dam steam removal","desc":"Low-pressure steamer with operator; shingle-safe ice removal at eaves and valleys","unit":"HR","qty":4,"category":"emergency"}},{"code":"LAB TO1","qty":1.5},{"code":"RFG IWS","qty":1.5,"brandOptions":[{"label":"Ice & Water Shield (Standard)","code":"RFG IWS"},{"label":"TAMKO Moisture Guard","code":"RFG IWS-TAMKO"},{"label":"Ice & Water Shield High-Temp","code":"RFG IWS-HT"}]},{"code":"RFG 240-GAF-HDZ","qty":1.5,"brandOptions":[{"label":"GAF Timberline HDZ","code":"RFG 240-GAF-HDZ"},{"label":"Owens Corning Duration","code":"RFG 240-OC-DUR"},{"label":"CertainTeed Landmark Pro","code":"RFG 240-CT-LMP"}]},{"code":"RFG STRT","qty":40},{"code":"RFG DRPE-AL","qty":40,"optional":true},{"code":"SPC HC","qty":40,"optional":true},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_se_renail_qc","name":"Post-Storm Re-Nail & QC Certification","category":"storm_emergency","jobType":"repair","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"After a wind event, we re-fasten and hand-seal lifted shingles across your whole roof, then certify its condition with a documented quality inspection.","scopeNotes":"Whole-roof pass (sized for ~20 SQ): fastener upgrade to 6-nail pattern on lifted/under-nailed courses (CUP FNR), hand-sealing of lifted tabs (detail hours), full QC walk, dated photo certification set, and labor-warranty documentation the homeowner can show their carrier or a buyer. Good fit when damage is real but below claim threshold, or as post-repair certification. Excludes shingle replacement — if creased/torn shingles are found, convert to jt_se_wind_section_repair. Adjust CUP FNR qty to actual roof squares.","tags":["re-nail","wind","certification","qc","prevention"],"durationHint":"4-6 hours","minJobCharge":750,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2000,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":40,"eaveLf":60,"rakeLf":40,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":0,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB","qty":1},{"code":"CUP FNR","qty":20},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":3},{"code":"LAB WALK","qty":1},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"code":"WAR LAB","qty":1},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1,"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_se_supplement_docs","name":"Insurance Supplement Documentation Package","category":"storm_emergency","jobType":"inspection","warrantyKind":"none","description":"A detailed follow-up documentation package that itemizes storm damage your insurance company's first estimate missed, prepared and submitted to the carrier on your behalf.","scopeNotes":"Use when the carrier scope is short: site revisit, supplemental photo set keyed to the carrier's line items, detail hours to measure and itemize missed scope (drip edge, IWS code upgrades, steep/2-story charges, haul-off), and preparation/submission of the supplement to the carrier. RULE from the supplement flow: supplement work bills only after carrier response — set expectations accordingly. Pair with jt_se_adjuster_walk history and the original inspection photos. Excludes any physical repair work and engineering letters (PRM ENG separately if causation is disputed).","tags":["insurance","supplement","claim","documentation","storm"],"durationHint":"2-3 hours on-site","minJobCharge":350,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2000,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":40,"eaveLf":60,"rakeLf":40,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":0,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB","qty":1},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":3},{"custom":{"name":"Supplement report preparation & carrier submission","desc":"Line-item supplement write-up mapped to carrier scope, submitted with photo exhibits","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"documentation"}}]},
{"id":"jt_ex_vinyl_siding_repair_100sf","name":"Vinyl Siding Section Repair (~100 SF)","category":"exterior","jobType":"repair","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Replace a damaged section of vinyl siding (about 100 square feet) with new matching panels, including fresh moisture wrap behind the repair and clean trim work around the patched area.","scopeNotes":"Fixed-scope patch repair, one elevation, one story. Color match is best-effort against weathered siding — set that expectation up front. Excludes sheathing replacement beyond the optional carpentry hours, full-elevation residing, and painting. Upsell: full elevation replacement (jt_ex_siding_replace_elevation) if the existing siding is brittle or discontinued; add gutter/fascia work while staging is up.","tags":["siding","vinyl","repair","exterior"],"durationHint":"4-6 hours","minJobCharge":450,"measurements":{"rawSqft":100,"pitch":0,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Vinyl siding panels (D4, color-matched)","desc":"Remove damaged panels, install new double-4 vinyl siding panels, best-effort color match","unit":"SF","qty":100,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"House wrap patch","desc":"Weather-resistive barrier patched and taped behind repair area","unit":"SF","qty":100,"category":"exterior"}},{"code":"SFT J-CH","qty":24},{"code":"LAB CARP","qty":2,"optional":true},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_ex_siding_replace_elevation","name":"Siding Replacement — One Elevation","category":"exterior","jobType":"replacement","warrantyKind":"install_default","description":"Strip the siding from one full side of the home and install new vinyl siding with fresh house wrap, trim channels, corner posts, and drip caps over windows and doors.","scopeNotes":"Full-job template: rep enters real measurements; custom line quantities are seeded for a typical ~600 SF single elevation — edit them to the measured wall area in preconfirm. Dumpster trio is formula-gated; permit included (swap PRM RES-KY for Kentucky jobs). Excludes sheathing/rot repair (add LAB CARP hours), other elevations, soffit/fascia, and window replacement. Upsell: whole-house residing, gutter guards, soffit vent upgrade while wall is open.","tags":["siding","vinyl","replacement","elevation","exterior"],"durationHint":"2-3 days","minJobCharge":null,"measurements":null,"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Remove existing siding (one elevation)","desc":"Strip existing siding and trim to sheathing, inspect wall","unit":"SF","qty":600,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"House wrap (full elevation)","desc":"Weather-resistive barrier, taped seams and openings","unit":"SF","qty":600,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Vinyl siding panels (D4)","desc":"New double-4 vinyl siding, homeowner color selection","unit":"SF","qty":600,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Vinyl starter strip","desc":"Starter course at base of elevation","unit":"LF","qty":40,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Vinyl outside corner posts","desc":"Corner posts both ends of elevation","unit":"LF","qty":40,"category":"exterior"}},{"code":"SFT J-CH","qty":80},{"code":"SFT DC","qty":24},{"custom":{"name":"Utility mount blocks","desc":"Mounting blocks for lights, outlets, spigots, vents","unit":"EA","qty":4,"category":"exterior"}},{"code":"LND TRP-S","qty":4,"optional":true},{"code":"DSP 20YD"},{"code":"DSP 30YD"},{"code":"DSP 40YD"},{"code":"PRM RES-OH"},{"code":"LAB DEMOB"},{"code":"LAB CLN-M"}]},
{"id":"jt_ex_window_replace_1","name":"Window Replacement (1 EA)","category":"exterior","jobType":"install","warrantyKind":"install_default","description":"Remove one existing window and install a new vinyl replacement window, sealed and insulated, with the exterior trim wrapped in aluminum for a clean, maintenance-free finish.","scopeNotes":"Pocket/insert replacement into a sound existing frame, up to approx 36x60 double-hung. Excludes full-frame tear-out, rotted frame repair (add LAB CARP hours), interior trim painting, and egress/code upgrades. Price per opening — duplicate the line for multi-window jobs and consider volume pricing at 5+. Upsell: whole-side or whole-house window package, aluminum capping on remaining windows to match. PRE-1978 CHECK: on a pre-1978 home this is EPA RRP work at ANY size — window replacement is specifically excluded from the minor-repair exemption, so the square-footage threshold never rescues it. Confirm the firm's RRP certification before scoping.","tags":["window","replacement","install","exterior"],"durationHint":"2-4 hours","minJobCharge":400,"measurements":{"rawSqft":0,"pitch":0,"waste":1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Vinyl replacement window (double-hung)","desc":"Insert-style vinyl double-hung, low-E dual pane, up to 36x60, set plumb/square and fastened","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Aluminum trim capping","desc":"Bend and install aluminum coil wrap on exterior casing/brickmould","unit":"LF","qty":16,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Seal and insulate opening","desc":"Low-expansion foam at jambs, exterior-grade sealant perimeter","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"}},{"code":"SFT DC","qty":4},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_ex_entry_door_replace","name":"Entry Door Replacement","category":"exterior","jobType":"install","warrantyKind":"install_default","description":"Replace an existing entry door with a new pre-hung insulated fiberglass door, including fresh exterior trim, weather sealing, and adjustment for a smooth, draft-free fit.","scopeNotes":"Standard 36-in pre-hung fiberglass unit in an existing rough opening. Lockset line covers install of a mid-grade knob + deadbolt (homeowner-supplied hardware installs free — toggle off). Excludes rough-opening resizing, sidelites/transoms, storm doors, staining/painting the slab, and structural header work (add LAB CARP for jamb/subsill rot). Upsell: storm door, matching back-door replacement, smart lock hardware. PRE-1978 CHECK: pulling the old unit disturbs painted jamb and trim, so on a pre-1978 home this is EPA RRP work — confirm the firm's RRP certification and the exterior minor-repair threshold before scoping. No machine sanding without HEPA extraction.","tags":["door","entry","install","exterior"],"durationHint":"4-6 hours","minJobCharge":450,"measurements":{"rawSqft":0,"pitch":0,"waste":1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Pre-hung fiberglass entry door (36-in)","desc":"Insulated fiberglass slab, pre-hung frame with sill, set/shim/fasten, adjust for even reveal","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Exterior PVC brickmould trim","desc":"New cellular PVC brickmould, caulked and ready for paint","unit":"LF","qty":17,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Lockset and deadbolt install","desc":"Bore-and-fit mid-grade keyed knob and deadbolt, strike plates aligned","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"},"optional":true},{"code":"SFT DC","qty":4},{"code":"LAB CARP","qty":2,"optional":true},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_ex_deck_board_repair_10","name":"Deck Board Repair (~10 boards)","category":"exterior","jobType":"repair","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Remove up to ten damaged or rotted deck boards and install new pressure-treated boards, fastened with coated deck screws for a safe, solid walking surface.","scopeNotes":"Board swap only — up to 10 boards, max 12 ft each, 5/4x6 pressure-treated. New boards will not match weathered gray until they age; note it on the proposal. Excludes framing/joist repair beyond the optional carpentry hours, railing work, staining/sealing. If more than ~20% of boards are bad, pivot to jt_ex_deck_rebuild_100sf. Upsell: wash + seal package, railing tightening, joist flash tape while boards are up.","tags":["deck","repair","boards","exterior"],"durationHint":"2-4 hours","minJobCharge":400,"measurements":{"rawSqft":0,"pitch":0,"waste":1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Replace deck board (5/4x6 pressure-treated)","desc":"Pull damaged board, install new PT board up to 12 ft, screwed to existing joists","unit":"EA","qty":10,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Coated deck screws (job pack)","desc":"Exterior-rated coated screws for full repair area","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"}},{"code":"LAB CARP","qty":2,"optional":true},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_ex_deck_rebuild_100sf","name":"Small Deck Rebuild (~100 SF)","category":"exterior","jobType":"replacement","warrantyKind":"install_default","description":"Tear off a worn-out small deck down to the footings and rebuild it with new pressure-treated framing and decking, flashed at the house to protect against water damage.","scopeNotes":"Ground-level/low deck to approx 100 SF, reusing existing sound footings. Railing and stair lines are optional toggles — required by code if walking surface is 30-in+ above grade, so verify height on site. Permit line optional; check local requirements (swap PRM RES-KY in Kentucky). Excludes new footings/piers (add LAB STR hours), composite decking (requote materials), electrical, and staining. Two haul loads included — swap to a 10YD dumpster if access allows. Upsell: composite surface upgrade, privacy screen, under-deck grading.","tags":["deck","rebuild","replacement","exterior"],"durationHint":"2-3 days","minJobCharge":1500,"measurements":{"rawSqft":100,"pitch":0,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Demo existing deck","desc":"Tear off decking, framing, and hardware down to footings","unit":"SF","qty":100,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Pressure-treated framing (2x8 @ 16-in OC)","desc":"New PT joists, beam, and blocking on existing footings","unit":"SF","qty":100,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Pressure-treated decking (5/4x6)","desc":"New PT deck boards, screwed, consistent gapping","unit":"SF","qty":100,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Joist hangers and structural fasteners","desc":"Galvanized hangers, structural screws, hurricane ties as needed","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Ledger flashing and lag attachment","desc":"Flash ledger at house, re-lag with structural screws","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Pressure-treated railing (36-in)","desc":"PT posts, top/bottom rail, balusters at code spacing","unit":"LF","qty":20,"category":"exterior"},"optional":true},{"custom":{"name":"Stair section (3 treads)","desc":"PT stringers, treads, and toe rail to grade","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"},"optional":true},{"code":"PRM RES-OH","qty":1,"optional":true},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":2}]},
{"id":"jt_ex_fence_repair_2panel","name":"Fence Section Repair (2 panels)","category":"exterior","jobType":"repair","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Replace two damaged wood fence panels, and reset a broken post in fresh concrete if needed, so the fence line stands straight and secure again.","scopeNotes":"Two 6x8 stockade/privacy panels, wood only. Post line is an optional toggle — walk the line and check every post for rot at grade before quoting. New panels will not match weathered fence color; staining excluded. Excludes gates, chain-link/vinyl fence, and full-run replacement (5+ panels = requote as custom job). Upsell: full-line post inspection, gate re-hang, stain/seal package.","tags":["fence","repair","panels","wood","exterior"],"durationHint":"2-3 hours","minJobCharge":350,"measurements":{"rawSqft":0,"pitch":0,"waste":1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Wood privacy fence panel (6x8, replace)","desc":"Remove damaged panel, install new pre-built PT panel, fasten to posts","unit":"EA","qty":2,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Fence post replacement (4x4 PT, set in concrete)","desc":"Pull broken post, dig out footing, set new PT post in fast-set concrete","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"},"optional":true},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_ex_paint_touchup_pkg","name":"Exterior Paint Touch-Up Package","category":"exterior","jobType":"maintenance","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Freshen up peeling or faded spots around the exterior — trim, fascia, doors, and shutters — with scraping, sanding, spot-priming, caulking, and matched paint.","scopeNotes":"Spot touch-up package (about a day, one painter): prep hours + finish hours + 2 gallons. NOT a whole-house or whole-elevation paint job — if scattered spots exceed ~10, requote as custom. Color match is best-effort against faded paint; the optional color-match line covers a matched custom tint. Excludes lead-paint abatement (pre-1978 homes need RRP assessment), stucco/masonry coating, and second-story work needing staging. Upsell: pair with pressure wash package for better adhesion and finish.","tags":["paint","touchup","exterior","maintenance"],"durationHint":"4-8 hours","minJobCharge":350,"measurements":{"rawSqft":0,"pitch":0,"waste":1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Surface prep (scrape, sand, spot-prime, caulk)","desc":"Prep failing areas: scrape loose paint, sand edges, spot-prime bare wood, caulk gaps","unit":"HR","qty":3,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Exterior acrylic paint and primer","desc":"Premium exterior acrylic, matched to existing color","unit":"EA","qty":2,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Touch-up painting labor","desc":"Brush/roll finish coats on prepped areas, clean lines at edges","unit":"HR","qty":4,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Custom color match service","desc":"Chip-match and custom tint at supplier for discontinued colors","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"},"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_ex_pressure_wash_house_roof","name":"Pressure Wash — House + Roof Soft Wash","category":"exterior","jobType":"maintenance","warrantyKind":"none","description":"Wash the whole exterior: low-pressure soft wash of the siding and trim to lift dirt and mildew, plus a gentle roof treatment that kills algae and streaking without damaging shingles.","scopeNotes":"Single-family home to approx 2,500 SF exterior and 20 SQ roof. Roof line is SOFT WASH ONLY (SH mix) — never pressure-wash shingles; it voids manufacturer warranties. Shrub/landscape protection included — pre-wet and cover plantings near runoff. Excludes stain removal guarantees (rust/artillery fungus), window interior cleaning, and gutter interior clean-out. Upsell: driveway/walkway line, gutter brightening line, annual wash plan; great door-opener for a roof inspection while on site.","tags":["washing","softwash","roof","maintenance","exterior"],"durationHint":"4-6 hours","minJobCharge":400,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2000,"pitch":6,"waste":1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":0,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"House soft wash (siding and trim)","desc":"Low-pressure detergent wash of siding, trim, soffits; rinse windows","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"}},{"custom":{"name":"Roof soft wash treatment","desc":"SH-based algaecide soft wash, kills gloeocapsa magma streaking, no pressure on shingles","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"}},{"code":"LND TRP-S","qty":2},{"custom":{"name":"Driveway and walkway pressure wash","desc":"Surface-cleaner pass on concrete flatwork","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"},"optional":true},{"custom":{"name":"Gutter exterior brightening","desc":"Remove tiger-striping/oxidation from gutter faces","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"exterior"},"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_ex_chimney_tuckpoint_sf","name":"Chimney Masonry Tuckpoint (per SF)","category":"exterior","jobType":"repair","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Grind out failing mortar joints on the chimney and repack them with fresh color-matched mortar, restoring the brickwork so water stays out of the chimney and the roof below it.","scopeNotes":"Priced per SF of chimney face — default 40 SF (typical above-roofline chimney, all four faces). Adjust the tuckpoint qty to measured face area. Optional lines: reset counter flashing into fresh joints (strong add-on after grinding), crown repair, stainless cap, and breathable water repellent. Excludes brick replacement (quote LAB STR hours), full rebuild, flue liner work, and interior firebox. Roof protection around base included in mobilization. Upsell: crown + cap + sealer bundle — the full water-out package.","tags":["chimney","masonry","tuckpoint","repair"],"durationHint":"4-8 hours","minJobCharge":500,"measurements":{"rawSqft":0,"pitch":6,"waste":1,"ridgeLf":0,"eaveLf":0,"rakeLf":0,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":0,"wallLf":0,"pipes":0,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":0,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Grind and tuckpoint mortar joints","desc":"Grind joints to sound mortar (~3/4-in depth), repack with color-matched type-N mortar, tool joints","unit":"SF","qty":40,"category":"exterior"}},{"code":"RFG CNTR","qty":8,"optional":true},{"code":"SPC CHM-CR","qty":1,"optional":true},{"code":"SPC CHM-C","qty":1,"optional":true},{"custom":{"name":"Masonry water repellent sealer","desc":"Breathable siloxane repellent applied after mortar cure","unit":"SF","qty":40,"category":"exterior"},"optional":true},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_mt_annual_tuneup","name":"Annual Roof Tune-Up","category":"maintenance","jobType":"maintenance","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"A once-a-year checkup for your roof. We inspect the full roof surface, reseal exposed nail heads and small gaps, re-secure loose shingles, and sweep your yard for stray nails before we leave.","scopeNotes":"Covers up to 2 hrs on-roof detail work, a sealant/fastener kit, and an optional one-bundle shingle allowance (0.35 SQ) for spot replacements. Excludes flashing replacement, decking repair, and leak diagnosis beyond visual — quote roof_repair or leak_flashing templates for those. Upsell: maintenance plan enrollment, gutter visit same trip.","tags":["maintenance","tune-up","sealant","annual","preventative"],"durationHint":"2-3 hours","minJobCharge":450,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":44,"eaveLf":140,"rakeLf":60,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":30,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":2},{"custom":{"name":"Roof sealant & fastener kit","desc":"Roof-grade polyurethane sealant and ring-shank fasteners for resealing exposed nail heads and re-securing loose shingles","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"roofing"}},{"code":"RFG 240-GAF-HDZ","qty":0.35,"optional":true,"brandOptions":[{"label":"GAF Timberline HDZ","code":"RFG 240-GAF-HDZ"},{"label":"TAMKO Heritage","code":"RFG 240-TAMKO-HERITAGE"},{"label":"Owens Corning Duration","code":"RFG 240-OC-DUR"},{"label":"CertainTeed Landmark","code":"RFG 240-CT-LM"},{"label":"IKO Cambridge","code":"RFG 240-IKO"}]},{"code":"LAB CLN-M","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1,"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_mt_plan_visit_semiannual","name":"Roof Maintenance Plan Visit (Semi-Annual)","category":"maintenance","jobType":"maintenance","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"A scheduled visit under your roof maintenance plan. We check the roof surface, clear debris from valleys and around penetrations, touch up sealant where needed, and send you a photo condition report.","scopeNotes":"Per-visit scope for plan members — lighter than the Annual Tune-Up (1.5 hrs detail + 1 hr debris clearing, photo report included). No material replacement included; if boots or shingles are failing, quote a repair template. Upsell: upgrade to Annual Tune-Up, add Gutter Maintenance Plan Visit same trip.","tags":["maintenance","plan","semi-annual","photo-report"],"durationHint":"1-2 hours","minJobCharge":350,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":44,"eaveLf":140,"rakeLf":60,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":30,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":1.5},{"code":"DSP DBR-H","qty":1},{"custom":{"name":"Sealant touch-up kit","desc":"Roof-grade sealant for minor touch-ups at penetrations and exposed fasteners","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"roofing"}},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1,"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_mt_roof_certification","name":"Roof Certification Inspection (Real Estate)","category":"maintenance","jobType":"inspection","warrantyKind":"none","description":"A documented roof inspection for a home sale or purchase. We evaluate the full roof, flashings, and attic side, photograph everything, and provide a written certification letter stating the roof's condition and expected remaining life.","scopeNotes":"Real-estate transaction product — the deliverable is the signed certification letter (typically a 2-year certification when the roof qualifies). 2 hrs roof + attic inspection, photo documentation, report authoring. Excludes ALL repair work; if repairs are required to certify, quote them separately and schedule a re-inspection (add PRM REINS for the return trip). Upsell: Attic Moisture & Ventilation Inspection combo.","tags":["inspection","certification","real-estate","report"],"durationHint":"2-3 hours","minJobCharge":400,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":44,"eaveLf":140,"rakeLf":60,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":30,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":2},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"custom":{"name":"Roof certification letter","desc":"Written certification report with condition findings and remaining-life statement, signed by the inspecting contractor","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"inspection"}}]},
{"id":"jt_mt_gutter_plan_visit","name":"Gutter Maintenance Plan Visit","category":"maintenance","jobType":"maintenance","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"We clear all gutters and downspouts, flush-test the downspouts, re-secure loose hangers, and reseal leaking end caps and corners so water drains away from your home the way it should.","scopeNotes":"Sized for ~140 LF of gutter on a 1-story home: 2 hrs hand-clearing, 10 replacement hidden hangers for refastening, seam/end-cap reseal, debris hauled. Splash blocks are the optional adder. Excludes gutter or downspout section replacement and underground drain work — quote gutters_repair. Upsell: gutter guards (GTR GG-MESH / GTR GG-MIC), roof plan visit same trip.","tags":["gutters","maintenance","cleaning","plan"],"durationHint":"1-2 hours","minJobCharge":350,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":44,"eaveLf":140,"rakeLf":60,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":30,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"DSP DBR-H","qty":2},{"code":"GTR HNG-H","qty":10},{"custom":{"name":"Gutter seam & end-cap reseal","desc":"Gutter-grade sealant applied to leaking seams, miters, and end caps after cleaning","unit":"JOB","qty":1,"category":"gutters"}},{"code":"GTR SPLASH","qty":2,"optional":true},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_mt_moss_algae_treatment","name":"Moss & Algae Treatment","category":"maintenance","jobType":"maintenance","warrantyKind":"none","description":"We gently remove moss buildup from your shingles by hand, apply a roof-safe treatment that kills remaining moss and algae, and can install zinc strips at the ridge to keep growth from coming back.","scopeNotes":"Soft-wash/manual removal ONLY — never pressure-wash shingles. Sized for ~22 SQ of treated area; adjust the treatment qty to the actual roof. Zinc ridge strip is the prevention upsell (optional, sized to ridge LF). Set expectations on heavy lichen or granule-loss roofs: treatment will not restore lost granules — pivot to a replacement consult. Excludes gutter cleaning (add the Gutter Maintenance Plan Visit).","tags":["moss","algae","treatment","soft-wash","prevention"],"durationHint":"3-5 hours","minJobCharge":600,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":44,"eaveLf":140,"rakeLf":60,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":30,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"custom":{"name":"Moss & algae soft-wash treatment","desc":"Manual moss removal plus roof-safe algaecide and moss-killer application, per square","unit":"SQ","qty":22,"category":"roofing"}},{"custom":{"name":"Zinc anti-moss strip at ridge","desc":"Zinc strip installed along the ridge line to inhibit future moss and algae growth","unit":"LF","qty":44,"category":"roofing"},"optional":true},{"code":"DSP DBR-H","qty":1},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]},
{"id":"jt_mt_sealant_refresh_sweep","name":"Sealant Refresh Sweep (All Penetrations)","category":"maintenance","jobType":"maintenance","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"We inspect and reseal every roof penetration — pipe boots, vents, flashing edges, and exposed fasteners — with fresh roof-grade sealant to stop small leaks before they start.","scopeNotes":"Whole-roof sealant pass sized for a typical ranch (3 pipes, 1 chimney, misc vents — 3 hrs detail labor, 6 tubes). Worn or cracked pipe boots get retrofit sleeves (2 included as the optional line; swap the brand option to standard or lead boots when full replacement is warranted). NOT a substitute for flashing replacement — failing step/counter flashing goes to a leak_flashing template. Upsell: Annual Tune-Up plan enrollment.","tags":["sealant","penetrations","pipe-boot","preventative"],"durationHint":"2-4 hours","minJobCharge":450,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":44,"eaveLf":140,"rakeLf":60,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":30,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":3},{"custom":{"name":"Roof-grade sealant (tubes)","desc":"Polyurethane roof sealant tubes for boots, vents, flashing edges, and exposed fasteners","unit":"EA","qty":6,"category":"roofing"}},{"code":"RFG PIPE-RTR","qty":2,"optional":true,"brandOptions":[{"label":"Pipe Boot Retrofit Sleeve","code":"RFG PIPE-RTR"},{"label":"Pipe Boot Standard (Full Replacement)","code":"RFG PIPE-STD"},{"label":"Pipe Boot Lead (Full Replacement)","code":"RFG PIPE-LD"}]},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1,"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_mt_attic_vent_inspection","name":"Attic Moisture & Ventilation Inspection","category":"maintenance","jobType":"inspection","warrantyKind":"none","description":"We inspect your attic for moisture, staining, and insulation problems, take moisture readings, verify your intake and exhaust ventilation is balanced, and give you a written report with clear recommendations.","scopeNotes":"Attic-side inspection: 2 hrs including moisture-meter readings, ventilation NFA math against 1:150 / 1:300, baffle and insulation-blockage check, photo documentation. Deliverable is the written ventilation & moisture report. Excludes all corrective work — upsell paths: CUP VNT-R ventilation code upgrade, RFG SMT intake, RFG RIDG-VNT, and the ventilation category templates. Requires attic access; confirm hatch location at booking.","tags":["attic","ventilation","moisture","inspection","report"],"durationHint":"1-2 hours","minJobCharge":350,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":44,"eaveLf":140,"rakeLf":60,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":30,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":2},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"custom":{"name":"Ventilation & moisture report","desc":"Written report covering moisture readings, ventilation calculations, and corrective recommendations","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"inspection"}}]},
{"id":"jt_mt_warranty_compliance","name":"Warranty Compliance Inspection","category":"maintenance","jobType":"inspection","warrantyKind":"none","description":"We inspect your roof against the manufacturer's warranty requirements, document its condition with photos, and take care of the paperwork that keeps your coverage intact.","scopeNotes":"For roofs under manufacturer warranty (GAF System Plus, TAMKO, etc.) — verifies ventilation, accessory use, and condition items that can void coverage. WAR MFG covers the registration/records update; the optional WAR LAB line adds our labor-warranty documentation. If deficiencies are found, quote corrective work separately BEFORE they become claim denials. Note: we are GAF Certified (System Plus).","tags":["warranty","inspection","compliance","documentation"],"durationHint":"1-2 hours","minJobCharge":350,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":44,"eaveLf":140,"rakeLf":60,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":30,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":1.5},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"code":"WAR MFG","qty":1},{"code":"WAR LAB","qty":1,"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_mt_solar_ready_assessment","name":"Solar Panel-Ready Roof Assessment","category":"maintenance","jobType":"inspection","warrantyKind":"none","description":"Thinking about solar? We evaluate whether your roof is ready for panels: shingle condition and remaining life, decking and structure, attachment areas, and anything that should be fixed first — all in a written readiness report.","scopeNotes":"Pre-solar due diligence: 2 hrs roof + attic structural review, photo documentation, written readiness report (remaining-life estimate, attachment-zone notes, recommended pre-solar repairs). Optional PRM ENG line = stamped engineering letter when the solar installer or AHJ requires one. KEY UPSELL: if the roof has under ~10 years left, pitch the reroof BEFORE panels go on — removing and reinstalling panels later costs the homeowner far more.","tags":["solar","assessment","inspection","structural","report"],"durationHint":"2-3 hours","minJobCharge":450,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":44,"eaveLf":140,"rakeLf":60,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":30,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":2},{"code":"LAB PHOTO","qty":1},{"custom":{"name":"Solar readiness report","desc":"Written assessment covering remaining roof life, structural notes, attachment zones, and pre-solar recommendations","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"inspection"}},{"code":"PRM ENG","qty":1,"optional":true}]},
{"id":"jt_mt_winterization_package","name":"Preventative Winterization Package","category":"maintenance","jobType":"maintenance","warrantyKind":"repair","description":"Get your roof ready for winter. We clear gutters, valleys, and drains, reseal vulnerable penetrations and exposed fasteners, check flashings and shingles, and can add heat cable at the eaves to stop ice dams.","scopeNotes":"Fall-season bundle: 2 hrs debris clearing (gutters, valleys, drains) + 2 hrs sealant/fastener/flashing check. Heat cable (SPC HC) is the ice-dam prevention upsell — 40 LF default at eaves and valleys, size to actual eave exposure. Excludes ice & water shield retrofit (reroof-time item) and gutter guard installs (quote gutters_install). Pairs well with the Attic Ventilation Inspection — poor ventilation is the root cause of most ice dams.","tags":["winterization","ice-dam","seasonal","preventative","maintenance"],"durationHint":"3-5 hours","minJobCharge":600,"measurements":{"rawSqft":2200,"pitch":6,"waste":1.1,"ridgeLf":44,"eaveLf":140,"rakeLf":60,"hipLf":0,"valleyLf":20,"wallLf":30,"pipes":3,"chimneys":1,"skylights":0,"stories":1,"tearOffLayers":1,"deckReplacePct":0,"cutUpRoof":false},"items":[{"code":"LAB MOB"},{"code":"DSP DBR-H","qty":2},{"code":"LAB DTL-HR","qty":2},{"custom":{"name":"Winter sealant & fastener kit","desc":"Roof-grade sealant and fasteners for pre-winter touch-ups at penetrations and exposed nail heads","unit":"EA","qty":1,"category":"roofing"}},{"code":"SPC HC","qty":40,"optional":true},{"code":"DSP HAUL","qty":1}]}
